  "articleBody": "Replacing bathroom flooring is usually straightforward when the layout stays the same, but the correct scope depends on moisture exposure, subfloor condition, material choice, and whether plumbing or electrical work is included. A professional estimate should separate demolition, substrate repairs, waterproofing, flooring, trim, disposal, permits if applicable, and final inspection requirements.",
